  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Summertime** (1 other source): JP Biondo and Roy Williams joined in on this song [2]\n- **Steam Powered Aeroplane** (1 other source): Billy Failing sang the vocals on this one [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Steam Powered Aeroplane**: rare: 10 archived performances [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2018-05-02.litz.sbd.schoepsMK21.flac24** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 12 songs; 96 min [1]\n- **BillyStrings2018-05-02.SBD.Flac16**: soundboard; 12 songs; 96 min [3]\n- **billystrings2018-05-02.litz.sbd.schoepsMK21.flac16**: matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 12 songs; 96 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- JP Biondo and Roy Williams opened the show with their own set [3]\n- Band did not leave the stage before the encore Slow Train because of a hard curfew [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2018-05-02.litz.sbd.schoepsMK21.flac24**: taped by Keith Litzenberger; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Soundboard + Schoeps MK21's>Sound Devices 788t [1]. Also: Soundboard feed combined with Schoeps MK21 mics placed on stage directly in front of Billy, recorded on a Sound Devices 788t at 24-bit/48kHz; Mixed in Nuendo 4, fades in Sound Forge Pro 11, tracked with CDWAV, converted to FLAC with Trader's Little Helper [1]\n- **BillyStrings2018-05-02.SBD.Flac16**: taped by Rich Stoler; transferred by Rich Stoler; source: SBD > Tascam DR-100(24bit/48kHz) [3]. Also: Soundboard patch from Keith Litz, recorded to TASCAM DR-100mkII at 24-bit/48kHz, then dithered to 16-bit in Audacity and converted to FLAC [3]\n- **billystrings2018-05-02.litz.sbd.schoepsMK21.flac16**: taped by Keith Litzenberger; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Soundboard + Schoeps MK21's>Sound Devices 788t [2]",
